<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,145,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,145,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, meal exports in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 11/13/96    11/06/96	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 30,145,000  29,898,000    27,885,000</p>
<p> Capacity-X	34,476,000  34,476,000    33,569,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	34,668,921  34,668,921	     N/A</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 132,305     152,604	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   11/13/96    11/06/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,321,000   5,108,000     4,981,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,838,000   4,953,000     4,520,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  5,143,000   4,980,000     4,891,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,209,000   3,262,000     2,859,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,185,000   4,238,000     3,650,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,224,000   5,091,000     5,001,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,226,000   2,266,000     1,983,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	30,145,000  29,898,000    27,885,000</p>
</text>
